      "how_a_star_actually_forms_in_4_steps": "How a star actually forms (in 4 steps): ",
      "how_bright_the_object_looks_from_earth": "How bright the object LOOKS from Earth. Depends on both how much light the object emits AND how far away it is. A bright nearby star and a dim distant star can have the same apparent magnitude.",
      "how_bright_the_object_would_appear_if_": "How bright the object would APPEAR if placed at a standard distance of 10 parsecs (32.6 light-years). Lets us compare the actual luminosity of stars regardless of distance.",
      "how_comet_tails_actually_work": "How comet tails actually work",
      "how_dark_is_your_sky_most_people_live_": "How dark is your sky? Most people live under sky much brighter than they realize. The Bortle scale (1-9) ranks sky darkness; class 1 is true wilderness dark sky, class 9 is inner city. Where do you live?",
      "how_magnetars_make_frbs": "How magnetars make FRBs",
      "how_often": "How often",
      "how_the_instrument_works": "How the instrument works",
      "how_the_sun_shines": "How the Sun shines",
