      "carbs_3": "Carbs",
      "carbs_30_55_within_the_broader_balance": "Carbs 30–55%. Within the broader balanced range; the full Dietary Guidelines for Americans AMDR for carbs is 45–65%, so the upper end of this bucket and the start of \"high-carb\" both still fall inside DGA. Sustainable for most people.",
      "carbs_4": "Carbs",
      "carbs_55_75_the_55_65_segment_is_squar": "Carbs 55–75%. The 55–65% segment is squarely within the DGA AMDR. The 65–75% segment is the endurance-athlete or traditional Asian-rice-based pattern; fine with fiber + protein.",
      "carbs_75_with_low_fiber_high_glycemic_": "Carbs >75% with low fiber → high glycemic load. Common in heavily-processed snack-dominated days, but well above the US average (NHANES puts US carb intake at ~46–50%).",
